title: Rising Corruption
tags: event
view-if: flag_rising_corruption = 1 and rising_corruption_ticker_timer <= 0
on-arrival: {! 

    Q.flag_rising_corruption = 0; 
    if (Q.corruption < 60)
    {
        Q.rising_corruption_ticker_timer = 8;
    }  
    else
    {
        Q.rising_corruption_ticker_timer = 4;
    }

!}


= Corruption is Rising

Whispers in the press and on the floor of Congress grow louder: the party's dealings with patronage, contracts, and party financiers are drawing scrutiny. [? if corruption >= 60 : What began as murmurs has curdled into open accusation -== even allies concede the administration looks the part of a machine bought and paid for. ?][? if corruption < 60 : Nothing has broken into open scandal yet, but reformers and rivals alike sense an opening. ?]

How do we respond?

- @investigate: Order an internal investigation and clean house.
- @scapegoat: Quietly remove a minor official and call it accountability.
- @downplay: Deny there is any problem.

@investigate
subtitle: -2 Budget
choose-if: budget >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the budget for a real investigation.
on-arrival: budget -= 2; corruption -= 6; conservative_dissent += 3; liberal_strength += 2; PoliticalCostPenalty += 1; civil_service_act_available = 1 if civil_service_commission = 1

We order a genuine internal review, removing officials and renegotiating contracts tied to the worst abuses. It costs us allies among the machine's beneficiaries, but reformers and the press take notice.

@scapegoat
subtitle: -1 Budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; corruption -= 2; liberal_dissent -= 1; rising_corruption_ticker_timer = 4

A minor official is quietly shown the door. It buys a news cycle of "action taken," but everyone in Washington understands the machine itself is untouched. [? if corruption >= 60 : The respite will not last long. ?]

@downplay
on-arrival: liberal_dissent += 3; conservative_strength += 1

We dismiss the reporting as partisan noise and change the subject. Reformers seethe, but nothing costs us today - only later.